---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getSite } from '../lib/site';

const { tmsUrl: tmsBase } = getSite();
---
<Layout
  title="Solutions"
  description="Bycon solutions — transport management for NEMT and broker operations."
>
  <h1 style="font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em;">Solutions</h1>
  <p style="color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 2rem; max-width: 40rem;">
    What we ship today, and room to grow. Each product line gets its own experience at a dedicated URL.
  </p>

  <article
    style="background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.25rem; max-width: 42rem; box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(15,23,42,0.04);"
  >
    <h2 style="margin: 0 0 0.35rem; font-size: 1.25rem;">Transport management (TMS)</h2>
    <p style="margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9375rem;">
      A transport management system aimed at <strong>non-emergency medical transportation (NEMT)</strong> and similar broker-led networks—where
      documentation, timeliness, and defensible trip history matter as much as the route itself.
    </p>

    <h3 style="font-size: 0.8125rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--muted); margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem;">
      What operators gain
    </h3>
    <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1.15rem; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.9375rem;">
      <li style="margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
        <strong>Compliance &amp; audit posture</strong> — fewer documentation gaps; workflows that support Medicaid-style scrutiny and audit readiness.
      </li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
        <strong>Broker KPIs</strong> — clearer visibility into on-time performance, completion, and service quality so teams can manage to the numbers.
      </li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
        <strong>Standardized trip data</strong> — consistent trip logs, structured pickup/dropoff context, and a cleaner record of what happened in the field.
      </li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 0">
        <strong>Day-to-day operations</strong> — client messaging to support completion, replanning when reality diverges from the plan, and room to extend as you grow.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin: 1.5rem 0 0;">
      <a
        href={tmsBase}
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        style="display: inline-block; padding: 0.55rem 1rem; background: var(--accent); color: #fff !important; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.875rem;"
      >
        Open TMS
      </a>
      <span style="display: inline-block; margin-left: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--muted);">
        ({tmsBase.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '')})
      </span>
    </p>
  </article>

  <p style="margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--muted);">
    Additional products will appear here as they launch—same company, separate URLs where it makes sense.
  </p>
</Layout>
